<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Holliday returns for his adult preventive visit five weeks after his end-of-treatment review. He finished all 182 doses of tuberculosis treatment and has had no cough, fever, night sweats, or weight loss since. He is working full days at the dental office. He has kept to one or two drinks once a week, with no evening of heavy drinking since the spring, and he still sees his substance-use counselor once a month. He completed the health risk assessment before the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Adult preventive visit, age 22</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Pulmonary tuberculosis, treatment completed; alcohol use disorder, mild, improving</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None since tuberculosis treatment ended</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; working full days</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, much better than at the start of the year</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Shares an apartment with a roommate; friends nearby; work going well</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>One or two drinks once a week (AUDIT-C 3); no tobacco or other drugs; plays cards on weekends, home by midnight</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Three meals a day; weight up 8 kg since diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks to work; no other exercise</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all</td></tr><tr><td>Occupational</td><td>Dentist; wears a surgical mask and eye protection with every patient and an N95 respirator for aerosol-generating procedures in patients with suspected tuberculosis</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>About seven hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; no firearms at home; smoke detector working</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No concerns; vision normal at the end of ethambutol</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

