    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given. PHQ-2 0. AUDIT-C 3, below the risk threshold for men. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Pulmonary tuberculosis, treatment completed (A15.0)</content>. No symptoms of relapse. [S]<list><item>Yearly symptom screen at work instead of a skin or blood test, which would stay positive.</item><item>Same-day visit for cough lasting more than two weeks, fever, night sweats, or weight loss.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, mild, improving (F10.10)</content>. Drinking within low-risk limits since the spring. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide. [S]<list><item>Continue monthly counseling for three more months, then as needed.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today; recommended for health-care personnel</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Not immune at diagnosis (surface antigen and surface antibody negative). First of two HepB-CpG doses today; second in one month; surface antibody one to two months after the second dose, as for all health-care personnel</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, 2026-2027</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended; he will get it at his pharmacy</td></tr><tr><td>Measles, mumps, rubella and varicella immunity</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two documented doses of each in his childhood record, as required for health-care personnel</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap about four years ago</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Series completed in adolescence by his report</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Negative at the tuberculosis diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Antibody negative at the tuberculosis diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Tuberculosis screening at work</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>A skin or blood test stays positive after tuberculosis; a yearly symptom screen replaces it</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 3, below the risk threshold; counseling continues</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/72 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>BMI 20.8 with no risk factors; HbA1c 5.2 percent at diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health and STI screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Discussed privately; no screening indicated by his history; condoms discussed</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season; Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 1 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Immunization of health-care personnel: recommendations of the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices (ACIP) (2011)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Second hepatitis B dose in one month at a nurse visit, and surface antibody one to two months after it. Next preventive visit in one year. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

